Subject: [M156] [webvtt] Make text-track pseudo-elements read-only

Original change's description:
> [webvtt] Make text-track pseudo-elements read-only
>
> Add `-webkit-user-modify: read-only !important` to the
> `video::-webkit-media-text-track-*` rules in `mediaControls.css` so
> author CSS cannot make internal WebVTT text-track elements in the user
> agent shadow root editable or focusable.
>
> Most other user agent shadow pseudo-elements in `html.css` and
> `input_multiple_fields.css` already set `-webkit-user-modify: read-only
> !important`.
>
> While it is also possible to enforce this in C++, pinning the property
> in the UA stylesheet is a safer and lower-risk fix for backporting.
>
